# Bug Backlog — {{PROJECT}}

Real bugs found during work but not fixed in the current task (a genuinely-out-of-scope defect, never a way to hide required work). Re-triaged at every sprint-close / whole-app sweep: each OPEN row is fix-now / still-deferred + why / obsolete.

**A false-passing test is NEVER a backlog row** (test-intent §4) — it's a P0 fixed the moment it's found. Same for an exploitable-now security or {{DOMAIN_NOUN}} finding.

## Format
```
### <ID> — <one-line symptom>
- **Status:** OPEN | FIXED (<commit/PR>) | OBSOLETE
- **Symptom:** what's visibly wrong.
- **Suspected/root cause:** if known (traced to file:line), else "unknown — needs investigation".
- **Validation needed:** the test/smoke that would prove the fix.
- **Tier:** exploitable-now (fix this turn — should not be here) | deferred (+ why genuinely out of scope now).
- **Found:** <date> · <how it surfaced (which agent/lens/sweep)>
```

